     8	    """Recolor the two diagonal foreground-bar orientations, assigning teal to the larger orientation and red to the smaller one.
     9	
    10	    Input structure
    11	    - The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground color.
    12	    - Foreground pixels form one-cell-thick diagonal bars.
    13	    - Every foreground pixel belongs to exactly one diagonal orientation.
    14	
    15	    Rule
    16	    - Keep the background unchanged.
    17	    - Classify each foreground pixel by whether it has a diagonal neighbor on the NW/SE axis or the NE/SW axis.
    18	    - Recolor the orientation with more foreground pixels teal and the other orientation red.
    19	
    20	    Key insight
    21	    - The output colors depend on the relative population of the two diagonal orientations, not on a fixed slash direction or position.
    22	    """
